\DOC PROLOGUE_SUBROUTINE_SIM_TAC

\TYPE {PROLOGUE_SUBROUTINE_SIM_TAC : thm -> term list -> term -> int -> string list -> tactic}

\SYNOPSIS
Steps an {eventually}-form machine goal forward across a subroutine call,
instantiating a correctness theorem for the callee and replacing the symbolic
state in the assumptions with a later one carrying the callee's postcondition.

\DESCRIBE
The arguments are {corth : thm}, the subroutine correctness theorem used to
discharge the call; {inargs : term list}, the terms (register and memory reads
in the pre-state) supplying that theorem's input parameters; {outarg : term}, a
memory read in the post-state naming the subroutine's result; {m : int}, a
count of additional instructions to step (values from 0 upwards occur); and
{inouts : string list}, the names used for the result and the input operands
when the new assumptions are generated. Exactly one subgoal always results. In
the conclusion, the state argument of {eventually} is advanced from the current
state variable {sk} to a fresh later one {sk'}, the body of the {eventually}
predicate being unchanged. In the assumptions, the block describing the old
state — program-counter, stack-pointer, register and memory-read equations, the
loaded-program assumption and the accumulated {MAYCHANGE} relation (or, at the
start of a proof, a trivial reflexive {MAYCHANGE}) — is deleted and re-asserted
for the new state, with the {MAYCHANGE} relation extended by the components the
call may clobber, with new assumptions recording the callee's arguments and
return address, and with an added implication expressing the subroutine's
result value under its input bounds; previously derived result implications are
retained, sometimes re-ordered, and non-state side conditions such as the
nonoverlapping hypotheses are kept.
{
   A, state-facts(sk) ?- eventually ... sk
   =================================================================  PROLOGUE_SUBROUTINE_SIM_TAC corth inargs outarg m inouts
   A, result-facts, state-facts(sk') ?- eventually ... sk'
}
\noindent where {result-facts} comprises the retained result implications plus
one new one.

\COMMENTS
The observed traces show only this single kind of forward step, all on goals of
this {eventually} machine-correctness shape.

\ENDDOC
